// Package httpx is the small HTTP toolkit the generated API and business
// modules share.
//
// It owns three things and nothing else:
//
//   - the default JSON response envelope, {code, msg, data}, and the writers
//     that emit it (JSON, Error) next to the raw writers for responses that must
//     stay unwrapped (RawJSON, RawText, Bytes, NoContent);
//   - typed request binding (DecodeJSON, QueryInt, BindQuery) with a configurable
//     body limit, a content-type check, single-value and unknown-field rejection
//     and an optional code-first validator callback, plus the Router and typed
//     endpoint helpers (Get, Post, NoInput, ...) that bind and respond for a
//     handler;
//   - the composable net/http middleware and the three middlewares the generated
//     server installs by default (RequestID, AccessLog, Recover), alongside the
//     named route policies a module references and the composition root defines.
//
// It uses the standard library and the project's logging interface. It does not
// import the project's go-validate rules: binding takes a validator
// callback, so a DTO wires its validation in without this package knowing
// about it, and it defines no policy names of its own.
package httpx
